# A CANDIDATE: THE LIVE ENGINE b190673dbdbf AND ONE FIX (2026-11-25).
# Staged 0013 said "a refused pool commit fails the request" and did not: on
# the card, with 0016's switch, the backend process ended at its first refusal
# (München, 2026-11-25; docs/notes/room-on-the-card.md §4). The refusal was a
# std::exception, and the op that asked for the memory catches those and
# aborts. 0018 makes it a type nothing but the graph's own catch can take.
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-refusal.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# engine-next.series, line for line, then:
#   0018  the pool's refusal is not a std::exception: it reaches the graph
# With every switch off it must gate as b190673dbdbf does, fingerprint for
# fingerprint, or it rolls back. Its own test is 0016's row: a reranker copy
# with GGML_SYCL_POOL_REFUSE=2 against a control — the first two requests
# that grow the pool answered with an error by the SAME process, the third
# served with the control's scores.
